# SDDK Local-Only Artifact Policy (v3.5)
#
# Lines prefixed with `#` are comments. Paths listed here are GENERATED by
# the SDDK kernel during its phases (explore, propose, spec, design, tasks,
# apply, verify, debt-verify, archive, release). They are written to disk on
# the local machine and used by SDDK phase agents as their work surface.
#
# IMPORTANT — three things this file does NOT do:
#   1. It does NOT delete artifacts. They live on disk and are read by SDDK.
#   2. It does NOT hide artifacts from SDDK agents. The companion `.ignore`
#      file in the same project root re-includes these paths for ripgrep /
#      opencode `grep` / `glob` / `Read` tools. See `.ignore`.
#   3. It does NOT prevent SDDK from using these paths as Phase | Step inputs.
#      The contract is: **gitignored, but locally readable and writable.**
#
# Ref: prompts/sdd-kernel/git-contract.md § Local-Only Artifact Policy
# Ref: https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/dev/packages/web/src/content/docs/tools.mdx

# --- SDDK-generated directories (these are entirely SDDK content) ---
sddk/
openspec/changes/
openspec/changes/archive/
.atl/

# --- SDDK-generated files under docs/ ---
# (Leave other docs/* files — READMEs, CONTRIBUTING.md, etc. — committed.)
docs/ROADMAP.md
docs/ROADMAP.local.*
docs/adr/
docs/reports/
docs/metrics/

# --- SDDK runtime state ---
**/apply-checkpoint.json
sddk-config.json
sddk.local.*
.sddk/
